# .dockerignore — trim the build context sent to the Docker daemon.
#
# Stage 0 §6 (todo.md). The Dockerfile has no COPY step (the repo is
# bind-mounted at runtime by docker-compose, not baked into the image), so this
# only shrinks the context tarball uploaded on `docker compose build` — it does
# NOT affect what the running container sees through the /workspace mount.
#
# Excluding these avoids shipping large, machine-local trees (git history and
# the dev caches can be hundreds of MB) on every image build.

# Version-control metadata — never needed to build the image.
.git/
.gitignore

# .NET build output (regenerated inside the container).
bin/
obj/

# Host-owned HOME + NuGet/.NET/XDG caches created by the dev service.
.cache/

# IDE / tooling scratch.
*.user
.vs/
.idea/
